  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Bug fixes\n\n- Concurrent first reads of a class property return the base getter's value (#483, closes #479). An auto-property on a class target starts from its base getter's value: the first read stores base.Prop. The getter decided whether a read was the first by re-reading the read count after incrementing it, so two first reads made at the same time could both skip the base getter and return default. The shared PropertyValue<T> now seeds the value once under a lock, and every first read gets the base value. A single-threaded program behaves as before. A throwing base getter is still called only once, and a base getter that reads its own property still gets default from that nested read. Span properties now use PropertyValue<T> as well, so their imposters no longer contain a nested DefaultPropertyBehaviour class.\n\nPerformance\n\n- A method call records one history entry instead of three objects (#455, closes #406). A call used to allocate an arguments object, a history entry and a stack node. Its inputs now go straight into the history entry, and verification walks the recorded entries without allocating. With setup costs spread over 1,000 calls:\n\n  | Call | 1.0.9 | 1.0.10 |\n  | --- | ---: | ---: |\n  | Non-generic | 16.84 ns, 97 B | 8.66 ns, 49 B |\n  | Generic | 26.67 ns, 121 B | 15.23 ns, 41 B |\n  | Span | 22.09 ns, 137 B | 12.85 ns, 89 B |\n  | in struct, 8 candidate setups | 72.00 ns, 229 B | 40.47 ns, 181 B |\n\n  Verifying 1,000 recorded calls no longer allocates (it took 72 B before) and runs 3 to 6 times faster. The public arguments classes, history interfaces and Matches/As members stay source-compatible.\n- Ordinary properties generate much less code (#454, first phase of #407). Outcome sequences, callbacks, invocation counts and history, verification, and base-accessor handling now live in the shared PropertyGetter<T>, PropertySetter<T> and PropertyValue<T> types of Imposter.Abstractions. They are no longer repeated in every imposter. A single-property imposter drops from 390 to 261 lines and from 1,342 to 362 bytes of method IL, and a mixed workload generates about 7% less code. The fluent setup API is unchanged.\n- The generator's source cache no longer keeps the sources of removed registrations (#451, closes #450). Cached sources are dropped once no registration generates under their name, so editing registrations over time doesn't grow the cache.\n\nHousekeeping\n\nCleanups with no change to behaviour: a generated indexer setter's MarkConfigured is now private (#447), CodeQL findings in the generator and the test fixtures are fixed (#448, #445, #446), the legacy binary-serialization members of MissingImposterException are removed (#444), and the thread-safety tests share one helper (#449). Also an unused syntax helper is removed (#452) and the span allocation of a same-type generic call has a test budget (#453).",
